          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Supergeometry is the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"}> higher
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+topos"} base topos
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoints
            modeled on the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+object"} line object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            in there.
          %p
            As ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            studies spaces –
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifolds
            – that locally look like
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector spaces
